 These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Usage reporting
+
+`afterModelResponse` receives the sum of every provider call's usage reported in the turn rather than the most recent round's alone: a deployer billing or budgeting from this hook therefore receives the full cost of the turn, including every tool round ([validated by: reports 660 total tokens for a turn of two tool rounds and a final answer](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L42)).
+
+A turn with no tool calls is unchanged: it reports exactly what the single provider call reported ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
+A round that reports no usage is skipped rather than zeroing the sum; only rounds that reported are counted, and a turn where no round reported sends `undefined` to the hook ([validated by: sums the rounds that reported to 60 tokens and reports undefined when no round reported](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L52)).
+
+Usage is accumulated field by field via `addUsage`: `addUsage(undefined, undefined)` returns `undefined`, `addUsage(a, undefined)` or `addUsage(undefined, b)` returns the defined side, and `addUsage(a, b)` sums `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` ([validated by: returns undefined when both sides are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L11); [validated by: returns the defined side when the other is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L15); [validated by: sums all fields when both sides are defined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L23)).
